WEBVTT

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:23.980
"December 11th 8:00 AM
22 Hours Till Launch"

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:26.980
"Albinar Cosmodrome"

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:48.170
While in flight, you'll go
by the call sign, "Lycoris."

00:00:48.170 --> 00:00:50.000
Lycoris?

00:00:50.000 --> 00:00:51.800
One of the mission objectives

00:00:51.800 --> 00:00:57.430
is to test if voice transmissions
can be received from space.

00:00:57.430 --> 00:01:00.430
Here's the text you'll be reading.

00:01:00.600 --> 00:01:02.020
"Lycoris Cooking Show"

00:01:02.020 --> 00:01:04.230
"Lycoris Cooking Show"
"Lycoris Cooking Show"?

00:01:04.230 --> 00:01:11.690
You're to read the borscht recipe if you
experience no health issues in zero-G.

00:01:11.690 --> 00:01:14.650
If you're unwell,
read the cheeseburger one.

00:01:15.860 --> 00:01:20.240
This wasn't in the mock launch.
Why the recipes?

00:01:20.240 --> 00:01:22.450
It's like a codeword.

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:30.250
What do you think will happen if the UK
intercepts your transmission from space?

00:01:30.250 --> 00:01:31.290
Hmm?

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:36.880
They'll suspect we're sending
someone to space in secret.

00:01:36.880 --> 00:01:41.220
But with a recipe,
they'll think it's a cooking show.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:44.060
Such secrecy.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.230
This is important.

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:52.270
When in the air, say nothing but
the recipe until communications are cut.

00:01:52.270 --> 00:01:55.650
You saw the bomb
during mock launch, right?

00:01:55.650 --> 00:01:59.030
Yes. Beneath the seat.

00:02:02.240 --> 00:02:06.870
Don't do anything unless
instructed to, understand?

00:02:34.940 --> 00:02:37.360
"10:00 PM
8 Hours Until Launch"

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.700
"10:00 PM
8 Hours Until Launch"
It won't be long till launch.

00:02:45.910 --> 00:02:49.000
You're... Natalia?!

00:03:04.930 --> 00:03:11.440
"Irina: The Vampire Cosmonaut"

00:04:20.960 --> 00:04:26.800
"Lycoris Cooking Show"

00:04:27.430 --> 00:04:30.430
"December 12th 3:00 AM
3 Hours Till Launch"

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:40.730
"Albinar Cosmodrome - Launch Pad"

00:04:41.860 --> 00:04:44.320
"3:35 AM
2 Hours 25 Minutes Till Launch"

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:45.700
Here.

00:04:45.700 --> 00:04:47.280
Thanks.

00:04:47.280 --> 00:04:50.330
Hey! You can't bring that along!

00:04:50.330 --> 00:04:52.450
Let go!

00:04:56.370 --> 00:04:58.590
Hand over the stone!

00:04:58.590 --> 00:04:59.590
Wait!

00:05:00.630 --> 00:05:02.840
Huh?

00:05:02.840 --> 00:05:04.050
Lev!

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:10.390
They made what happened
the other day go away.

00:05:10.390 --> 00:05:14.350
The centrifuge wasn't broken,
it was meant to hurt you.

00:05:14.350 --> 00:05:15.350
What?

00:05:15.350 --> 00:05:17.560
I was told the truth.

00:05:17.560 --> 00:05:20.360
The one responsible was Franz.

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:23.030
Huh? Why would Franz do that?

00:05:23.030 --> 00:05:26.610
Someone opposing the chief ordered him to.

00:05:26.610 --> 00:05:32.870
If N44 died, the plan would fail
and the chief would be demoted.

00:05:32.870 --> 00:05:35.210
What will happen to Franz?

00:05:35.210 --> 00:05:40.290
No record of such a person exists here.

00:05:40.290 --> 00:05:42.630
That's unbelievable.

00:05:42.630 --> 00:05:48.220
That's the kind of country we're in.
Anyway, I'm glad I can see the launch.

00:05:48.220 --> 00:05:50.010
Thanks for the necklace.

00:05:50.010 --> 00:05:54.100
I know you wanna take it,
but let me hold on to it.

00:05:54.100 --> 00:05:56.390
All right.

00:05:56.390 --> 00:06:03.690
Though if a day comes that you go
to the moon, take it with you.

00:06:03.690 --> 00:06:08.320
Sorry. No can do.

00:06:08.320 --> 00:06:11.120
I-I see.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:13.620
'Cuz you'll be taking it there.

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:14.830
Huh?

00:06:18.580 --> 00:06:20.790
Wh-What?

00:06:24.340 --> 00:06:26.090
I've got it!

00:06:29.930 --> 00:06:33.430
Now you won't be mistaken as an enemy.

00:06:36.680 --> 00:06:38.890
It's time. Move out.

00:06:39.020 --> 00:06:41.520
"4:00 AM
2 Hours Till Launch"

00:06:46.570 --> 00:06:48.280
There's your ride.

00:06:56.410 --> 00:06:59.160
Lev, thanks for all your work.

00:06:59.160 --> 00:07:00.210
Yes, sir.

00:07:00.210 --> 00:07:05.250
Lycoris, board the cabin.
After the final checks, we'll launch.

00:07:05.250 --> 00:07:08.050
It'll be in 108 minutes.

00:07:08.050 --> 00:07:09.550
Yes, sir!

00:07:09.550 --> 00:07:12.090
You've become a fine cosmonaut.

00:07:12.090 --> 00:07:14.550
Thanks to my fine teacher.

00:07:32.570 --> 00:07:37.660
This might be goodbye
to this planet... and Lev.

00:07:37.660 --> 00:07:42.080
No, I'll return... I will.

00:07:46.380 --> 00:07:49.340
"4:50 AM
70 Minutes Till Launch"

00:07:49.510 --> 00:07:53.800
No mistakes. Our success
depends on all of you.

00:07:53.800 --> 00:07:56.300
Everyone, stay focused!

00:07:56.300 --> 00:07:59.470
Polnoc, this is Lycoris.

00:07:59.470 --> 00:08:01.690
Polnoc here. Go ahead.

00:08:01.690 --> 00:08:03.980
Comm tests are complete.

00:08:03.980 --> 00:08:06.060
One hour till launch.

00:08:06.060 --> 00:08:08.570
We're wrapping up final tests.

00:08:08.570 --> 00:08:09.780
Roger.

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:12.700
Cabin pressure is normal.

00:08:12.700 --> 00:08:14.450
Thirty minutes till launch.

00:08:14.450 --> 00:08:19.370
Heart rate: 64.
Respiratory: 24. No issues.

00:08:19.370 --> 00:08:22.290
Fifteen minutes till launch.

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.630
Lycoris, we're running a little late.

00:08:25.630 --> 00:08:28.920
Don't worry. All launches go like this.

00:08:28.920 --> 00:08:30.050
Roger.

00:08:30.050 --> 00:08:35.340
We'll ignite once final checks are
complete. There won't be a countdown.

00:08:35.340 --> 00:08:39.100
Roger. Preparing for launch.

00:08:39.100 --> 00:08:40.680
Final checks!

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:42.640
Range finder, go.

00:08:42.640 --> 00:08:44.440
Comms, go.

00:08:44.440 --> 00:08:46.650
Propulsion, go.

00:08:46.650 --> 00:08:48.400
All systems, go!

00:08:48.400 --> 00:08:49.690
Set keys!

00:08:49.690 --> 00:08:51.990
Keys set!

00:08:51.990 --> 00:08:53.530
Ignition sequence!

00:08:56.200 --> 00:08:57.530
Preliminary stage!

00:09:01.450 --> 00:09:02.870
Intermediate stage!

00:09:06.040 --> 00:09:08.460
Lycoris, hold on tight.

00:09:08.460 --> 00:09:09.590
Roger!

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:13.510
Engine ignition!

00:09:13.510 --> 00:09:14.670
Main combustion!

00:09:14.670 --> 00:09:16.260
Engines firing.

00:09:19.260 --> 00:09:20.390
Launch!

00:09:30.610 --> 00:09:32.650
Irina... Go!

00:09:49.540 --> 00:09:51.590
Yes! She made it!

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:52.840
Yippee!

00:09:55.470 --> 00:09:59.800
Silence! The real deal starts now!

00:09:59.800 --> 00:10:03.680
Altitude: 4,000... 5,000!

00:10:03.680 --> 00:10:09.060
Tracking the rocket.
Position and acceleration look good.

00:10:09.060 --> 00:10:11.860
Engine temp and pressure, normal.

00:10:17.900 --> 00:10:20.950
It doesn't affect the flight. Fix it.

00:10:21.950 --> 00:10:23.660
First stage separation.

00:10:24.950 --> 00:10:28.080
Cabin temp maintaining 20 degrees.

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.590
Wh-What?! Heart rate is 150!
Breathing is rapid!

00:10:33.590 --> 00:10:34.670
Not good!

00:10:34.670 --> 00:10:35.510
What?!

00:10:35.510 --> 00:10:38.550
Shoot! She'll lose consciousness!

00:10:38.550 --> 00:10:44.720
This is Polnoc! Lycoris, what's the
recipe?! Respond, Lycoris! Lycoris!

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:47.980
No response? Are we connected?

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.640
We should be.

00:10:49.640 --> 00:10:53.520
Lycoris! Do you copy? What's the recipe?!

00:10:53.520 --> 00:10:55.480
95,000!

00:10:55.480 --> 00:10:57.650
Respond, Lycoris!

00:10:57.650 --> 00:11:01.700
100,000! 101,000!

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.870
Altitude broke ten kilos.

00:11:03.870 --> 00:11:06.370
Fairing jettison.

00:11:06.370 --> 00:11:09.370
Flight is maintaining course.

00:11:09.370 --> 00:11:11.750
Second stage jettison.

00:11:11.750 --> 00:11:14.540
Third stage ignition.

00:11:14.540 --> 00:11:16.170
Where's the picture?!

00:11:16.170 --> 00:11:18.380
Still investigating.

00:11:18.380 --> 00:11:22.220
Third stage burn complete.
Third stage jettison.

00:11:22.220 --> 00:11:25.810
Altitude stable. Orbital velocity reached.

00:11:25.810 --> 00:11:27.680
Launch was successful!

00:11:30.190 --> 00:11:34.110
Lycoris! Is it borscht or cheeseburger?!

00:11:34.110 --> 00:11:36.980
Did her brains get scrambled?

00:11:36.980 --> 00:11:39.530
Is she dead?

00:11:39.530 --> 00:11:40.860
No...!

00:11:58.550 --> 00:12:01.930
I'm...? Huh, what?

00:12:01.930 --> 00:12:03.590
Lycoris! Which recipe?!

00:12:03.590 --> 00:12:06.300
Huh? Uh, right!

00:12:06.300 --> 00:12:10.480
Today's recipe is... borscht!

00:12:14.440 --> 00:12:16.730
Borscht! It's borscht!

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.070
Yeah!

00:12:18.070 --> 00:12:20.490
--Yay!
--Woohoo!

00:12:33.920 --> 00:12:37.960
Th-This is the Lycoris Cooking Show!

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:44.590
First, peel your carrots, potato, and
beets and cut into bite-size portions.

00:12:44.590 --> 00:12:49.220
Then dice some cabbage
and slice the onions as well.

00:12:49.220 --> 00:12:54.560
Next, heat oil in a pot
and sauté the meat.

00:12:54.560 --> 00:13:00.110
Add the salt, carrots, and celery.
And once they soften up,

00:13:00.110 --> 00:13:03.280
add water and half a quartered tomato.

00:13:03.280 --> 00:13:09.910
Add bay leaves, consommé, and season
to taste, simmering for an hour.

00:13:09.910 --> 00:13:14.960
Next, add the rest of the veggies
and simmer for 20 more minutes.

00:13:14.960 --> 00:13:18.840
Keep the heat low
so the potatoes don't overcook.

00:13:25.930 --> 00:13:30.430
While that's simmering,
prepare your sour cream.

00:13:30.430 --> 00:13:33.980
At this point, you can taste and plate.

00:13:33.980 --> 00:13:39.020
Sprinkle some parsley if desired,
and your tasty borscht is complete!

00:13:39.020 --> 00:13:41.110
All done! Enjoy!

00:13:43.030 --> 00:13:49.240
It's a success so far, but don't lose
focus! Re-entry is full of challenges!

00:13:56.290 --> 00:13:57.790
So beautiful.

00:13:59.500 --> 00:14:03.380
I really did make it to space...

00:14:04.960 --> 00:14:07.220
That's where I lived...

00:14:10.850 --> 00:14:16.270
To think, I can't even talk about
what I'm feeling right now...

00:14:16.270 --> 00:14:23.980
I want to tell Lev what it feels like
to float... and how pretty the view is.

00:14:23.980 --> 00:14:27.280
Hmm? A recipe!

00:14:27.280 --> 00:14:30.950
Next, a drink to pair with your borscht!

00:14:30.950 --> 00:14:35.950
Huh? A drink?! We gave no such orders!

00:14:35.950 --> 00:14:37.620
Is it spy code?!

00:14:37.620 --> 00:14:40.880
Comrade Chief, standby with the bomb.

00:14:40.880 --> 00:14:43.920
I recommend oleaster <i>nastoyka</i>.

00:14:43.920 --> 00:14:46.380
--<i>Nastoyka? </i>Huh?
--Drop rock sugar on oleaster
in a cup and fill it with <i>zhizni</i>.

00:14:46.380 --> 00:14:48.970
--Drop rock sugar on oleaster
in a cup and fill it with <i>zhizni</i>.

00:14:48.970 --> 00:14:50.720
--<i>Nastoyka</i>'s a flavor of our motherland,
just like borscht. It's all right.
--Drop rock sugar on oleaster
in a cup and fill it with <i>zhizni</i>.

00:14:50.720 --> 00:14:54.850
--<i>Nastoyka</i>'s a flavor of our motherland,
just like borscht. It's all right.
--Add some cotton thistle
as a secret ingredient!

00:14:54.850 --> 00:15:00.600
--She prefers booze over blood?
You're vampire's a drunkard.
--But not too much! Then give it a lid
and put it somewhere dark.

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:03.520
--Begging for her life by humoring us?
--Let it infuse for at least three weeks
so it tastes nice and mellow!

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:04.270
--Huh?
--Let it infuse for at least three weeks
so it tastes nice and mellow!

00:15:04.270 --> 00:15:05.900
--She's not begging for her life. Only us
two know about oleaster <i>nastoyka</i>.
--Let it infuse for at least three weeks
so it tastes nice and mellow!

00:15:05.900 --> 00:15:10.360
--She's not begging for her life. Only us
two know about oleaster <i>nastoyka</i>.
--It'll turn red and delicious! But it's
alcohol, so don't give it to kids.

00:15:10.360 --> 00:15:12.160
--It'll turn red and delicious! But it's
alcohol, so don't give it to kids.

00:15:12.160 --> 00:15:13.490
--Instead, give 'em lemon seltzer!

00:15:13.490 --> 00:15:14.990
--Lemon seltzer!
--Instead, give 'em lemon seltzer!

00:15:20.460 --> 00:15:23.000
"7:05 AM
58 Minutes After Launch"

00:15:38.430 --> 00:15:40.980
Sinus Iridum...

00:15:40.980 --> 00:15:43.650
Lacus Somniorum...

00:15:43.650 --> 00:15:46.190
Palus Somni...

00:15:46.190 --> 00:15:48.530
Oceanus Procellarum...

00:15:50.780 --> 00:15:54.780
Going to the moon...
is an impossible dream.

00:16:13.590 --> 00:16:15.470
I don't wanna die.

00:16:16.350 --> 00:16:18.810
"7:26 AM
79 Minutes After Launch"

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:21.310
"Transition to Atmosphere Re-entry Phase"

00:16:30.360 --> 00:16:32.530
Compared to training, this is nothing!

00:16:34.240 --> 00:16:36.620
It's no use! We can't restore comms!

00:16:36.620 --> 00:16:39.330
Why?! We're past re-entry blackout!

00:16:39.330 --> 00:16:42.500
The cable was cut!
Could be antenna damage!

00:16:42.500 --> 00:16:44.210
What else is wrong?!

00:16:44.210 --> 00:16:50.210
Temperature rising! The heat shield
may be flawed! It might burn or break up!

00:16:53.680 --> 00:16:55.220
Irina! Answer me!

00:16:55.220 --> 00:16:57.220
Hey! Don't interfere!

00:16:57.220 --> 00:16:58.560
Irina!

00:16:58.560 --> 00:17:02.100
Where will it fall?!
If it's not our land, blow it up!

00:17:02.100 --> 00:17:06.190
No, it's in our borders,
but retrofiring wasn't perfect.

00:17:06.190 --> 00:17:10.280
It's 100 kilometers off course,
so it'll be hard to locate.

00:17:10.280 --> 00:17:13.190
Chief! Can I assist with the search?!

00:17:13.190 --> 00:17:15.320
Mmm. Of course.

00:17:15.320 --> 00:17:17.530
Viktor! Aid in the search.

00:17:17.530 --> 00:17:18.530
Yes, sir!

00:17:20.870 --> 00:17:28.460
The landing area is the 100 kilometers
around latitude 51.6, longitude 47.4.

00:17:28.460 --> 00:17:33.300
The search team is struggling.
N44's status is unknown.

00:17:33.970 --> 00:17:36.970
"Local Time: 3:01 PM"

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:23.520
The seat was ejected.

00:18:24.970 --> 00:18:26.390
Which means...!

00:18:28.440 --> 00:18:31.980
Irina!

00:18:31.980 --> 00:18:34.480
Irina!

00:18:40.700 --> 00:18:46.080
I've gotta find her before dark,
'cuz by that time, she'll...

00:19:12.650 --> 00:19:18.150
I thought she was a vampire,
but she's an ordinary girl.

00:19:18.150 --> 00:19:23.950
One that hates people, is stubborn,
and gets upset when teased.

00:19:28.200 --> 00:19:32.170
When did I start seeing her
as a normal person?

00:19:35.920 --> 00:19:40.220
This is the first manned
spaceflight in history. Enjoy it.

00:19:44.720 --> 00:19:46.220
Be back soon.

00:19:51.940 --> 00:19:53.440
"Local Time: 4:50 PM"

00:19:56.230 --> 00:19:57.440
What's that?

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:11.750
Irina!

00:20:14.210 --> 00:20:17.800
And she's conscious? Well done, Lev!

00:20:24.680 --> 00:20:27.560
Affirmative. We'll head there immediately.

00:20:32.560 --> 00:20:36.310
I... came back.

00:20:36.310 --> 00:20:40.900
Yeah. All the way from space.

00:20:40.900 --> 00:20:44.530
Let's wait it out till help comes.

00:20:44.530 --> 00:20:46.830
Lev, you're bleeding.

00:20:46.830 --> 00:20:48.410
It's no big deal.

00:20:48.410 --> 00:20:49.830
So stubborn.

00:20:49.830 --> 00:20:51.330
You're one to talk.

00:20:58.380 --> 00:21:01.670
Your <i>nastoyka </i>reached me loud and clear.

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:03.260
I'm glad.

00:21:24.280 --> 00:21:26.070
Thank goodness you're safe.

00:21:27.530 --> 00:21:30.370
Welcome home, Irina.

00:21:32.910 --> 00:21:35.960
I'm home, Lev.

00:21:37.830 --> 00:21:44.840
Her amazing feat may never
be known by anyone in the future.

00:21:44.840 --> 00:21:51.470
She'll never receive any praise,
nor will her name go down in history.

00:21:51.470 --> 00:21:56.940
Much the opposite--her existence
will be swept into the shadows.

00:21:58.360 --> 00:22:01.440
But the truth is different--

00:22:01.440 --> 00:22:05.950
She was the world's very first cosmonaut.

00:23:49.260 --> 00:23:50.970
"Next Episode:
'A Maiden's Prayer'"
